package skill

// AnalysisErrorGranularityTeaching is shared by analyzer skill and tool schema.
// It describes one existing classification, not a second answer-shape field.
const AnalysisErrorGranularityTeaching = "Emit error_granularity_profile on every call with is_granularity_question and confidence. Set false unless the CURRENT request asks how failure propagates across an item, record, call, batch, transaction, or sibling set. Event inventories, recording processes/threads, event order, and causal relationships near a failure are not themselves a failure-scope verdict. True asks whether a bad member is rejected while valid siblings continue, the whole operation fails, a mixed result is returned, processing stops at the first error, or errors accumulate. The profile requests investigation; it never predicts its result. When true, quote only the actual failure-scope subquestion in source_quotes. In a mixed cause-plus-scope request, retain both independent questions; do not reuse an event/actor/causal dimension's quote to invent another obligation, and do not add a duplicate presentation row just to activate this profile. Unresolved or differently quoted classifications remain subject to evidence, not lexical rules."

const AnalysisErrorGranularityOptionsTeaching = "requested_verdict_options contains only alternatives explicitly proposed by the user: per_item_rejection, whole_batch_failure, partial_success, fail_fast, collect_errors. Two or more distinct options form a requested contrast. A single option is a yes/no proposition, not an affirmative answer or a closed choice set: grounded evidence may establish a different verdict. Omit options when none is named; never infer an option from failure logs or expected results. not_enough_evidence is only a final-answer verdict."
